==Enemy==
Red Cyclone deals absurd damage and attacks non-stop, destroying anything it touches in less than a second. However, it has one of the shortest ranges in the game, somewhat slow speed, and two exploitable traits.

==Strategy==
Because of its extreme DPS, the use of [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]]/[[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] units with crowd-control abilities ([[:Category:Cats with Freeze ability|freeze]], [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|slow]] or [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|knockback]]) are absolutely necessary to impede it. Examples include [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bodhisattva Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] and [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]]. Just be warned that if you only use Pirate Cat and/or Fortune Teller Cat for knockback effects, your stack will gradually clip into Red Cyclone as it gets knocked back and potentially die all at once unless Red Cyclone can be quickly frozen/defeated before it attacks.

In Floors 21 of the [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 21|Heavenly]] and [[Infernal Tower/Floor 21|Infernal]] Towers, things are made slightly more complicated by the addition of [[Christmas D.|Christmas Ds]] that can wipe out your stacks, so use [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]] to knock them back behind the frontlines, or longer-ranged crowd-control options backed by meatshields that stall these enemies briefly.

