==Variants ==
{{Variant
|original = Red Cyclone
|Dark Cyclone
|Its damage per hit is quite low, but its 20% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] Cat Units somewhat makes up for it. However, Dark Cyclone itself gets knocked back up to 10 times. It appears in [[Attack on D-Cyclone (Expert)|Heaven of Darkness]] and [[NEO Darkness Heaven]].
|White Cyclone
|Very similar to Red Cyclone in terms of stats, but with more knockbacks. Its lack of a secondary trait may make it slightly harder to counter than the previous Cyclones. It appears in [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Peerless]] and [[Peerless Too]].
|Divine Cyclone
|The first non-[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] Cyclone; units such as [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Stilts Cat]], [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Toaster]] and [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]] are needed to keep it at bay. It appears in [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Wrath of Heaven]] and [[Wrath of the Divine]].
|Metal Cyclone
|It has the highest health of any [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy, making [[Critical Hit]]s a necessity to defeat it. Moves very slowly, and has as many knockbacks as [[Dark Cyclone]]. It appears in [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Sweet Irony]] and [[Bitter Irony]].
|Cosmic Cyclone
|It has significantly longer range than most Cyclones, though not enough to reach [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] or [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]], and strengthens by 200% at 30% health. It appears in [[Black Hole Rising (Insane)|Dimension of Despair]] and [[Dimension of Delirium]].
|The Perfect Cyclone
|Has extreme range and very high DPS compared to other enemies with similar range, although not much for a Cyclone. Due to its Long Distance ability, it is vulnerable to tanks with enough health and few enough knockbacks to enter its blind spot, like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]]. It appears in [[Oncoming Storm (Insane)|Red Sky at Morning]] and [[Red Sky at Night]].
|Zyclone
|A Cyclone that can revive with 100% health an unlimited number of times. To win against it, the player will need to defeat it with [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] or sneak units past it before it can revive. Unlike most [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], it can't burrow past Cat Units. It appears in [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)|The Rolling Dead]] and [[The Dead Keep Rolling]].
|Super Cosmic Cyclone
|This Cyclone is a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]], which means its difficulty will vary depending on one's [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. Its damage is fairly low regardless of Treasures, but it Warps cats back with every attack. It has even longer range than [[Cosmic Cyclone]]: enough to hit [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], but still not enough to reach [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]. It appears in [[The Wormhole Opens (Deadly)|The 2nd Dimension]] and [[The 3rd Dimension]].
|Primeval Cyclone
|A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] Cyclone that has the highest health and movement speed of any full-sized Cyclone, and increases its attack power by 200% after reaching 50% health. It appears in [[Charybdis' Mouth (Merciless)|Typhoon Nemo]] and [[Typhoon Nihil]].
|Mesocosmocyclone
|A very strong [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] peon that warps Cat Units ''forward'' with every hit, while also having fast movement speed, short range and non-stop attacks. As such, it can push at terrifying speeds when not met with crowd-controllers or [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]]. It appears in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3 and [[Legend Stages]].
|Li'l Zyclone
|A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemy that has high health and burrows far, but has somewhat low DPS; his main role is to intercept the flow of meatshields. Unlike [[Zyclone]], he can only revive once. He appears in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3 [[Zombie Outbreaks]] and [[Uncanny Legends]].
|Aku Cyclone
|Moves very slowly but has above-average range for a Cyclone, 4 knockbacks and a [[Shield]] with as much health as the Cyclone itself: 1,666,666, effectively giving it 8,333,330 HP. Topping this off is its [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait, leaving players with few reliable means of stalling it in its first appearance without [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]]. The only silver lining is that its damage per hit is relatively low compared to other Cyclones. It appears in [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]] and [[The Greatest Diablo]].
|Mini White Cyclone
|A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy with even higher health than [[Li'l Zyclone]] and 120k DPS, which is balanced out by single-target attacks and even lower speed than [[White Cyclone]]. He appears in [[Zero Legends]].
|Mini Angel Cyclone
|An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy that's not as deadly as [[Mesocosmocyclone]] nor as resilient as [[Li'l Zyclone]], but can potentially hit further and even more frequently than other Cyclones with a 25% chance of creating a level 1 [[Mini-Surge]] at 150-750 range. She appears in [[Zero Legends]].
|E-792
|A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that uses Long Distance attacks like [[The Perfect Cyclone]], but with shorter reach, standing range and damage. She also has a 100% chance to weaken units to 25% for 2 seconds, effectively perma-weakening them with her non-stop attacks. She appears in [[Zero Legends]].
}}

